  "reasoning": "PR #9907 is a ~2,670-line feature (24 sub-commits in one merge) that adds a whole runtime-pulled-image subsystem: ImageServiceManager/RuntimeServiceManager plus VM-specific ImageServer/RuntimeServer implementations (1,295 new lines in internal/storage alone), new datastore image-management APIs, and a cross-cutting API change from ContainerServer.StorageImageServer()/StorageRuntimeServer() (no args, single return) to (sandbox, error)-returning accessors, plus threading a storage.ImageServer through server.pullArguments and adding an sb parameter to addOCIBindMounts/verifyImageSignature/setPodSandboxMountLabel. Chain depth is 4: RuntimeServiceManager -> ImageServiceManager -> runtimePulledImageService -> datastore.Store -> libartifact.ArtifactStore. Good news: there are no new packages, no generated/binary content beyond one mockgen file, the internal/storage ImageServer/RuntimeServer interfaces and all their helpers are byte-identical between target and the fix's parent, and a trial cherry-pick produces only 6 conflicts \u2014 so the mechanical merge is easy and all 6 new internal/storage files land as-is. The real work is semantic, and matches the task brief: (a) internal/storage must be re-keyed from main's SandboxInfo-per-sandbox caches onto whatever 1.35-appropriate keying the resolver chooses (target's *sandbox.Sandbox already implements ID()+RuntimeHandler(), so storage.SandboxInfo can be kept as the fix defines it and used as-is, but the sandbox-removal cache eviction in RemoveSandbox has to be checked against 1.35's RemoveSandbox), and (b) internal/ociartifact/datastore is structurally different on 1.35 (target embeds *ociartifact.Store; main was rewritten by the out-of-tree 99520fec9), so the fix's PullManifestOnly/PullConfig/ImageSource/List/Remove must be re-implemented against target's Store and artifact.go dropped in favour of the existing ociartifact.Artifact \u2014 the upstream bodies will not compile verbatim (confirmed: `datastore.Store has no field or method PullManifestOnly/PullConfig/ImageSource`). Also expect freebsd/linux divergence (sandbox_run_freebsd.go, container_create_freebsd.go) which cannot be compiled here (the freebsd build is already broken by go.podman.io/common/libimage on this platform), and a mockgen file that must be regenerated (mockgen is not vendored; the target mock covers only Impl, not Impl+LibartifactStore). Skipping vars.yml/kata.yml is deliberate: those hunks are kata 3.31.0 / runc 1.5.1 / crun 1.29.1 / cri-tools v1.36.0 version bumps and peer-pods provisioning that belong to mainline CI and would regress the 1.35 prow job; kata-remote.bats and the Ansible changes cannot be validated here. container_events_test.go is a bundled unrelated test-only race fix (upstream e02bb25aa) for the ContainerEvents subsystem, not for image-server routing. Build/vet/test baselines were measured on pristine target (build clean ~11s; `go vet ./internal/...` clean; `go vet ./server/...` already exits 1 on pre-existing container_events copylocks findings, and one server RRO bats-less unit test already fails due to host mount propagation) \u2014 the restricted lint scope above is deliberately chosen to be clean before the backport so any new finding is attributable. Human review should focus on internal/ociartifact/datastore and on whether the runtime-pulled caches are keyed/evicted consistently in the 1.35 sandbox lifecycle. The single highest-risk file is internal/ociartifact/datastore/store.go: it is the only place where the two branches diverge structurally, and prerequisite_details records the exact resolution (embed-and-delegate to the existing *ociartifact.Store; port only PullManifestOnly/PullConfig/ImageSource; drop artifact.go; do not regenerate the datastore mock with the upstream Impl, which would break target's existing MockImpl-based store_test.go). Only ONE file is auto-skipped: test/mocks/ociartifact/datastore/datastore.go is mockgen output whose upstream form (MockImpl{NewArtifactReference,ReadFile} + MockLibartifactStore) does not match target's datastore.Impl, so it must be regenerated rather than resolved by hand. I deliberately did NOT auto-skip contrib/test/ci/vars.yml, contrib/test/ci/build/kata.yml, test/kata-remote.bats or server/container_events_test.go: kata.yml and kata-remote.bats are pure additions that apply cleanly (skipping them would only replace a clean 3-way merge with a wholesale --theirs copy), and vars.yml + container_events_test.go are the two files where 'take --theirs' is the wrong answer. vars.yml genuinely conflicts and the trial merge shows why: a naive resolution yields TWO kata_version keys (\"3.6.0\" and \"3.31.0\"), so the agent must keep release-1.35's kata/cri-tools/runc/crun pins and take only the new podvm_image/caa_image lines. server/container_events_test.go is an unrelated mainline test-race fix (upstream e02bb25aa) but it merges cleanly on its own; forcing --theirs would additionally drag in main-only content (GinkgoRecover in the recv closure) that release-1.35 does not have, so it is safer to leave it to the normal 3-way merge. None of these four files affect whether the backport compiles or what its unit tests assert."
}
