Compare the upstream fix against the applied diff. For every symbol (class, function, method, constant, import) that appears in the upstream fix but was removed or changed in the applied diff, run `git grep '<symbol>' a97127ed69ccdf89aef156d4a7d848b00ca8c72c` to check whether it actually exists on the port baseline.

If a symbol exists on the baseline but was removed from the port, the removal was wrong — restore it. If a symbol genuinely does not exist on the baseline, the adaptation was correct — leave it.

When checking whether a class has a particular method, check the full inheritance chain: find the class definition, read its parent class, and check whether the method is defined on any ancestor. Inherited methods count as available.

